Date: 10-1-89 Transmittal: UP-89-40 2510.45 page 2 ______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Categorical Eligibility Requirements POLICY ______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: AFDC Deprivation of Parental Support or Care ____________________________________________________________ Subject: Good Cause for Non-Compliance With Work Program Requirements ______________________________________________________________________________

2510.45 C. 1. Circumstances for Good Cause (continued)

b. illness of another household member;

c. if necessary child care is not available and payment cannot be guaranteed by the Department;

d. an emergency;

e. the unavailability of transportation;

2. conditions of employment, such as, but not limited to:

a. discrimination on the basis of age, sex or color;

b. working without being paid on schedule;

c. net loss of income as a result of accepting employment (cross-reference: 3510.07);

d. unsuitable employment.

D. Suitable Employment

The suitability of employment depends on some conditions related to the individual and some related to the particular job. A job is considered unsuitable when:

1. it is not within the documented physical and mental capability of the individual;

2. it interferes with the individual's religious beliefs of observances;

