3005.05 B. Eligible Non-citizens (continued)

a non-citizen granted voluntary departure whose departure the INS does not contemplate enforcing;

k. a non-citizen granted deferred action status;

l. a non-citizen residing in the U.S. under orders of supervision;

m. a non-citizen granted suspension of deportation and whose departure the INS does not contemplate enforcing;

n. a non-citizen whose deportation has been withheld;

o. any other non-citizen living in the U.S. with the knowledge and permission of the INS and whose departure the INS does not contemplate enforcing, including permanent non-immigrants and persons granted Extended Voluntary Departure due to conditions in the non-citizen's home country based on a determination by the Secretary of State; or

classified by the INS as a newly legalized non-citizen and meets certain requirements described at 3005.15; or

a North American Indian born in Canada who:

a. has maintained residence in the United States since entry; and

is at least one-half American Indian blood.

C. Non-citizens Eligible Due to a Medical Emergency

A non-citizen who does not fall into one of the categories listed in B is eligible for MA only, if he or she has an emergency medical condition.

