CONNECTICUT DEPARTMENT OF SOCIAL SERVICESPRIVATE UNIFORM POLICY MANUAL _______________________________________________________________________________ Date: 4-1-88 Transmittal: UP-88-21 3030.05 _______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Technical Eligibility Requirements POLICY _______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: AFDC Concurrent Assistance AABD _______________________________________________________________ FS Subject: MA Concurrent Programs _______________________________________________________________________________

3030.05 There is a technical requirement prohibiting the receipt of benefits from two financial assistance programs at the same time. In addition, AABD must be received concurrently with SSI or some countable income other than GA. The Food Stamp program also requires discontinuance of Food Stamp benefits in one state before assistance can be granted in another. Medicaid has no comparable requirements. Programs that can and cannot be received concurrently are as follows:

A. AFDC

An individual who is receiving AFDC:

1. may receive Food Stamps concurrently;

2. may receive AFDC concurrently with General Assistance (for treatment of the GA payment refer to Treatment of Income Section - 5000)

3. may not receive AFDC concurrently with any of the following:

a. Old Age Assistance;

b. Aid to the Blind;

c. Aid to the Disabled;

d. SSI.

4. may not separately receive Medicaid as medically needy;

5. may not receive AFDC as a member of another assistance unit simultaneously.

CONNECTICUT DEPARTMENT OF SOCIAL SERVICES UNIFORM POLICY MANUAL _______________________________________________________________________________ Date: 5-1-92 Transmittal: UP-92-11 3030.05 page 2 _______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Technical Eligibility Requirements POLICY _______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: AFDC Concurrent Assistance AABD _______________________________________________________________ FS Subject: MA Concurrent Programs _______________________________________________________________________________

3030.05 B. AABD

An individual who is eligible for State Supplement:

1. must be:

a. receiving SSI; or

b. receiving some other source of countable income in excess of the SSI amount for which the individual would qualify; or

c. have income deemed to him or her in excess of the SSI amount for which the individual would qualify;

2. may receive AABD concurrently with Food Stamps;

3. may not receive AABD concurrently with either:

a. AFDC; or

b. another category of State Supplement;

4. may not separately receive Medicaid as medically needy;

C. MA

An individual who is eligible for MA may receive MA concurrently with any of the following:

1. Food Stamps;

2. General Assistance;

3. AFDC;

4. AABD;

CONNECTICUT DEPARTMENT OF SOCIAL SERVICES UNIFORM POLICY MANUAL _______________________________________________________________________________ Date: 1-1-05 Transmittal: UP-05-02 3030.05 page 3 _______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Technical Eligibility Requirements POLICY _______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: AFDC Concurrent Assistance AABD _______________________________________________________________ FS Subject: MA Concurrent Programs _______________________________________________________________________________

3030.05 D. Food Stamps

An individual who is eligible for Food Stamps:

1. may receive any other program administered by the Department;

may receive benefits from the Puerto Rico Nutrition Assistance Program (cross reference 5050.10);

may not receive Food Stamps from another state or territory concurrently, except for a resident of a battered women's shelter.

CONNECTICUT DEPARTMENT OF INCOME MAINTENANCEPRIVATE UNIFORM POLICY MANUAL _______________________________________________________________________________ Date: 12-1-89 Transmittal: UP-89-45 P-3030.05 _______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Technical Eligibility Requirements PROCEDURES _______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: AFDC Concurrent Assistance _______________________________________________________________ Subject: Ensuring Appropriate Assistance _______________________________________________________________________________

P-3030.05 AFDC/SSI

1. When an individual qualifies for both AFDC and SSI:

° explain the programs to the individual;

° allow the individual to choose between the programs;

° include any mandatory assistance unit member in the AFDC unit while an SSI decision is pending;

° discontinue AFDC as soon as SSI is granted to the individual after proper notice.

2. Coordinate the effective date of one program with the discontinuance date of the other program.

Two AFDC Assistance Units

1. When an individual qualifies as an assistance unit member in two AFDC units:

° refer to assistance unit requirements (2000) to make sure there is a choice;

° explain to the individual the differences between being in one unit rather than the other.

2. When an eligible child moves from one active assistance unit to another:

° discontinue assistance to the child as of the end of the month he or she leaves the unit or the first month in which it is administratively possible to do so, whichever is later;

° grant assistance to the child as a member of the second unit as of the month following the month of discontinuance from the first unit.

CONNECTICUT DEPARTMENT OF INCOME MAINTENANCEPRIVATE UNIFORM POLICY MANUAL _______________________________________________________________________________ Date: 4-1-87 Transmittal: UP-87-1 P-3035.05 _______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Technical Eligibility Requirements PROCEDURES _______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: AFDC Striker Status _______________________________________________________________ Subject: AFDC Procedures for Active Cases _______________________________________________________________________________

P-3035.05 1. If a parent or the only eligible dependent child in the assistance unit is a striker:

° send a discontinuance notice for the last day of the month with a note that the action will be voided if the striker notifies us of a return to work before the last day of the month;

° institute recoupment of the entire month's benefits if the individual is on strike on the last day of the month;

° void the discontinuance if the striker returns to work before the last day of the month.

2. If eligibility of the assistance unit is not dependent on the striker:

° send a notice to remove the individual from the assistance unit effective the end of the month;

° compute an overpayment of the individual's share of the AFDC payment for the month;

° void both of the above actions if the striker returns to work before the last day of the month.

3. Check eligibility of assistance unit members for Medicaid.

CONNECTICUT DEPARTMENT OF INCOME MAINTENANCEPRIVATE UNIFORM POLICY MANUAL _______________________________________________________________________________ Date: 4-1-87 Transmittal: UP-87-1 3099.20 _______________________________________________________________________________ Section: Type: Technical Eligibility Requirements POLICY _______________________________________________________________________________ Chapter: Program: Verification Requirements FS _______________________________________________________________ Subject: Student Status _______________________________________________________________________________

3099.20 A. All students in institutions of higher education must verify school enrollment.

B. Each student must also verify any of the following which apply to this requirement and are pertinent to the student's individual situation:

1. age, including the age of children for whom support or care is claimed;

2. physical or mental disability;

3. hours of employment;

4. wages from employment, including self-employment;

5. participation in work-study.

C. A student whose claim to be enrolled in secondary school is questionable because of the student's age must verify enrollment.

D. A student who does not provide verification as required is ineligible.

