3510.10 A. Non‑medical Exemptions

All of the following members of the AFDC assistance unit are exempt from employment and training requirements except for registration:

1. a caretaker relative age 60 or over;

2. an individual under age 16;

except as specified in 3510.13, a parent or other caretaker relative responsible for the full‑time care of a dependent child under the age of 2, with only brief and infrequent absences from the child. A separation of 25 hours per week or less is considered brief and infrequent with the following qualifications:

if the caretaker relative is attending post‑secondary school full time, the separation is not considered brief and infrequent;

if the child is attending Headstart or kindergarten, the separation is considered brief and infrequent;

if the caretaker relative is separated from the child for the purpose of carrying out a responsibility related to the care of the dependent child, such as shopping for food or to meet a personal need, such as keeping a doctor's appointment, the absence is considered brief and infrequent;

a parent or other caretaker relative responsible for the full‑time care of a dependent child over the age of 2, but less than 6, with only brief and infrequent absences (as described in A.3) when:

a. the Department cannot assure that payment for child care is guaranteed; and

b. participation in the program exceeds twenty (20) hours per week;

an individual over the age of 16, but less than 19, who is in school full‑time or participating full‑time in one of the following:

a. an elementary school;

