P-4099.15 The following are examples of verifications that an asset is inaccessible:

1. document showing that someone else other than the assistance unit or deemor has to agree to liquidate a jointly held asset; and a statement from the other person that he or she is not willing or able to do so;

2. trust statement showing that the assistance unit must rely on the trustee to release funds to it; and a statement from the trustee showing that he or she does not intend to release funds to the unit (this is not true in the MA program, however);

