8055.30 A. Securing Support

The caretaker relative is required to cooperate in securing prior support obligations from legally liable relatives.

B. Termination of Employment

The caretaker relative must not stop employment without good cause.

C. Good Cause

Good cause for termination of employment by the caretaker relative is found if any of the conditions listed below are met.

1. The caretaker relative terminates employment due to circumstances beyond his or her control, such as the following:

a. illness;

b. illness of another household member;

c. necessary child care is not available, or payment cannot be guaranteed by the Department;

d. an emergency;

e. the inaccessibility of transportation.

2. The caretaker relative terminates employment due to conditions of employment, such as the following:

